   "response_text": "Everything checks out. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**What I changed (library source only, zero test files touched):**\n\n1. **`invkit/store.py`** \u2014 added `Inventory.total_value(category=None)`:\n   - No category \u2192 sums `item.value` (price \u00d7 quantity) over every item.\n   - Category given \u2192 delegates to the existing `by_category()`, so matching stays identical (strip + case-insensitive). DRY, no duplicated filtering logic. YAGNI respected \u2014 no extra params nobody asked for.\n   - Returns `round(..., 2)`.\n\n2. **`invkit/cli.py`** \u2014 added `--total` (`store_true`) and a final `print(f\"Total value: {inv.total_value():.2f}\")` after the report, so it always renders 2 decimals even for whole numbers (`215.00`, not `215.0`). The total is computed over the whole inventory, not the `--low`-filtered view.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `--total` prints the report then exactly one `Total value: 215.00` line (correct: 25\u00d73 + 0.10\u00d7500 + 7.50\u00d712).\n- `total_value(\"tools\")` == 165.0, and `\"  TOOLS \"` matches too, confirming `by_category` parity.\n- Without `--total`, output is unchanged.\n- `python -m pytest -q` \u2192 4 passed.\n\nDONE",
